{"name":"Cyprus Spring","hex":"#acb7b0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spring","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move or burst forth.","To appear."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of springing: a leap, a jump.","The season of the year in temperate regions in which temperatures and daylight hours rise, and plants spring from the ground and into bloom and dormant animals spring to life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spring"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cyprus","blocks":[{"text":"Cyprus, officially the Republic of Cyprus, is an island country in the eastern Mediterranean Sea, located off the coast of the Levant mainland in West Asia. The island of Cyprus, which is the third largest and third most populous island in the Mediterranean, is divided along the United Nations Buffer Zone between the internationally recognised Republic of Cyprus and the Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus, which is recognised only by Turkey. The south of the island also hosts the British sovereign military bases of Akrotiri and Dhekelia. The capital and largest city of Cyprus is Nicosia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Flag_of_Cyprus.svg/330px-Flag_of_Cyprus.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyprus"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Geology_of_Cyprus-SkiriotissaMine.jpg/500px-Geology_of_Cyprus-SkiriotissaMine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Geology_of_Cyprus-SkiriotissaMine.jpg/1280px-Geology_of_Cyprus-SkiriotissaMine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Geology_of_Cyprus-SkiriotissaMine.jpg/500px-Geology_of_Cyprus-SkiriotissaMine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A copper mine in Cyprus. In antiquity, Cyprus was a major source of copper.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeology_of_Cyprus-SkiriotissaMine.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Choirokoitia.jpg/500px-Choirokoitia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Choirokoitia.jpg/1280px-Choirokoitia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Choirokoitia.jpg/500px-Choirokoitia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Archaeological site of Khirokitia with early remains of human habitation during the Aceramic Neolithic period (reconstruction)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChoirokoitia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Kition%2C_Zeus_Keraunios.jpg/500px-Kition%2C_Zeus_Keraunios.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Kition%2C_Zeus_Keraunios.jpg/500px-Kition%2C_Zeus_Keraunios.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Zeus Keraunios, 500–480 BC, Nicosia museum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKition%2C_Zeus_Keraunios.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Kyrenia_01-2017_img11_Castle_exterior.jpg/500px-Kyrenia_01-2017_img11_Castle_exterior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Kyrenia_01-2017_img11_Castle_exterior.jpg/1280px-Kyrenia_01-2017_img11_Castle_exterior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Kyrenia_01-201